The authors thank the maintainers of \mbox{$\tau^3$}-bench and AgentChangeBench for the public task environments that motivate the production-stress evaluation harness in this paper. The main-matrix evidence in this paper was produced by driving a live Qwen3-8B endpoint served by vLLM 0.23.0 with the \texttt{SyncLLMClient} in \texttt{experiments/harness/llm.py} against the public \texttt{data/tau2/domains/\{airline,retail,telecom\}} and \texttt{data/simulations/\{airline,retail\}} task fixtures. Reproduction scripts live in \texttt{experiments/harness/run\_real\_external.py}, \texttt{aggregate\_suite.py}, \texttt{refresh\_paper\_artifacts.py}, and \texttt{audit\_results.py}. The full 1{,}392-row, 39-run matrix completes in approximately four hours on a single Qwen3-8B endpoint and is regenerated by running \texttt{./scripts/wait\_for\_gpu\_idle.sh} followed by \texttt{./scripts/finalize\_submission.sh}, or by following the runbook in \texttt{docs/aamas/experiment\_runbook.md}.
